<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">August 6, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 160 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-08-06T07:05:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.1</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
    <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Three forecasts moved materially today — <span class="cite">F2</span> (US-strike probability) from 24% to 12% as the August&nbsp;2 cancellation was absorbed with five days remaining; <span class="cite">F4</span> (Hormuz commercial-traffic recovery) from 20% to 8% on near-zero tanker transit data and unresolved structural barriers to normalization; and <span class="cite">F6</span> (Israeli right-bloc electoral outcome) from 22% to 13% on consistent polling placing the bloc eleven seats short of the 61-seat threshold — all three moving downward, with no forecast opening above its prior.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active &middot; F1 resolved AMBIGUOUS &middot; F8 new &middot; last reasoned 2026-08-06</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (&le;72h)</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast within 72 hours today. Next near-term: F2 resolves 2026-08-11 (5 days).</div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <!-- F2 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the United States military conduct confirmed new strikes against targets on Iranian soil before EOD 2026-08-11?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">12%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&Delta; &minus;12pp from 24% (2026-08-06)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-11</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No US strikes on Iranian sovereign territory Aug 4–6. Trump cancelled planned air campaign Aug 1 (confirmed: Axios/NPR/WaPo/CBS) — sixth consecutive night of post-cancellation pause. Bessent Aug 4–5 deal deadlines elapsed without strike or agreement. Iran Aug 6 stated US is "ready to return to commitments" under June 17 MOU, consistent with active backchannel communication. Five days remain. p moved 0.24 → 0.12.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Pentagon or CENTCOM confirms airstrikes, missile strikes, or special-operations raids against targets located within Iran's internationally recognized land borders before EOD 2026-08-11.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Pentagon/CENTCOM official statement on defense.gov, OR Reuters/AP/AFP with named DoD/CENTCOM confirmation.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Trump threat without confirmed execution = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Strikes on proxies in Iraq/Syria/Yemen = NO. Vessels at sea = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Pentagon/CENTCOM confirms strikes on Iranian soil</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC reports casualties from US strikes on Iranian territory</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F3 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a formal US–Iran negotiating session — direct or mediated by a named state mediator — be confirmed by both parties before EOD 2026-08-18?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&Delta; &minus;4pp from 26% (2026-08-06)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-18</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran MFA Aug 6 sustained Aug 3 denial: "path of understanding is between Iran and Oman." New element: Iran characterized US as "ready to return to commitments" under June 17 MOU — Iran's framing of US posture, not confirmation of a session. Qatar FM: "very progressive stages." Iran-Oman working group creates documented bilateral channel. Twelve days remain. p moved 0.26 → 0.22.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Reuters/AP reports — with named officials from both the US and Iran — that a face-to-face negotiating session was held before EOD 2026-08-18. Oman-Iran Hormuz track alone does NOT qualify unless US is a named party.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP with confirmation from named US representative AND named Iranian representative. One-sided US confirmation alone = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Trump assertion without Iranian MFA confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Written message exchanges or back-channel relays without a convened session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA explicitly confirms participation in mediated session with US</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Reuters/AP reports named US envoy met named Iranian envoy in third-country format</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F8 (new) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8 <span style="font-size:0.75em;color:var(--accent4);">NEW</span></span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran and Oman formally publish an operational Strait of Hormuz transit framework — including named service fees or a defined per-vessel cost structure — before EOD 2026-08-22?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (successor to F1)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-22</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast; direct successor to resolved F1. Aug 6 Iran-Oman joint communiqué established a joint working group with explicit mandate to determine "future administration of navigation, services and costs." 16-day horizon. Upward pressure: both governments committed, geographic route confirmed. Downward pressure: IRGC toll preference vs US rejection of any transit fee regime is a structural impasse; P&amp;I cover and US Navy posture unchanged.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Iran-Oman joint working group publicly releases a document naming specific service fees, per-vessel charges, or a defined cost schedule — with both governments' endorsement confirmed — before EOD 2026-08-22.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/Bloomberg/Al Jazeera) OR Oman ONA + Iran IRNA/Tasnim carrying the published fee schedule. Both governments must confirm or co-publish.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Fees "to be determined" or "in accordance with international standards" without published rates = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. US rejection does NOT affect resolution. Fee schedule for IRGC-supervised vessels only = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRNA + Oman ONA carry identical framework with named fee schedule</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Joint working group publishes named fee table</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <!-- F4 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will commercial shipping transits through the Strait of Hormuz reach &ge;30 vessels/day (7-day rolling average, IMF PortWatch) before EOD 2026-09-07?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">8%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&Delta; &minus;12pp from 20% (2026-08-06)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-07</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Kpler/AIS Jul 27–Aug 2: 106 all-vessel crossings (~15/day) — all-vessel, not commercial-transit count. TankerMap Aug 5: 0 tanker transits. Dark AIS 41%. P&amp;I war-risk cover suspended. Aug 6 corridor communiqué establishes route but names no fees; insurance normalization and shipper-confidence recovery have not occurred. 32 days remain. p moved 0.20 → 0.08.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch records 7-day rolling avg &ge;30 commercial vessel transits/day for any consecutive 7-day window ending before EOD 2026-09-07.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IMF PortWatch (portwatch.imf.org) primary. Lloyd's List Intelligence or Bloomberg shipping data as substitute; flag AMBIGUOUS if sources conflict &gt;20%.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Single-day spikes without qualifying 7-day average = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Naval-escorted convoys count. PortWatch unavailable &gt;3 consecutive days: extend horizon and flag AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IMF PortWatch 7-day avg rises above 20/day (leading indicator)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">P&amp;I war-risk insurance reinstated for Hormuz transit</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F5 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran agree to a verified freeze or transfer of its highly enriched uranium (&ge;60% enriched) stockpile as part of a binding framework before EOD 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">13%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">&Delta; 0pp (unchanged)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No material movement. IAEA lacks access to Isfahan underground HEU storage. June 2026 Switzerland talks established four working groups including Nuclear Affairs but no HEU freeze mechanism confirmed. Iran ballistic missile program "not for negotiation." Diplomatic focus entirely on Hormuz corridor. p=0.13 unchanged.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Iran officially agrees — in a written document co-signed or formally witnessed by IAEA or a named state guarantor — to either (a) a verified freeze of &ge;60% enriched UF6 stockpile with continuous IAEA monitoring, or (b) transfer of that stockpile to a named third country, before EOD 2026-10-27.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IAEA Director General's written report or official press statement as primary source, plus Reuters/AP confirmation. IRNA acknowledging the agreement alongside IAEA confirmation also qualifies.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Verbal commitment without signed, witnessed document = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Framework reducing enrichment rates without addressing existing HEU stocks = does NOT count. Provisional halt without IAEA continuous monitoring = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IAEA Director General confirms Iranian HEU freeze or transfer under verified framework</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran and US/P3+1 announce binding framework document witnessed by IAEA</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F7 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-regime status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F7 <span style="font-size:0.75em;color:var(--accent3);">⚑ REVIEW</span></span>
          <span class="fc-category">regime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Netanyahu's coalition formally lose its Knesset majority (below 61 seats via roll-call vote), or will the election date move earlier than 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">6%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">&Delta; 0pp (flagged — see notes)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No formal Knesset roll-call majority-loss vote confirmed. Knesset dissolved July 17 via consensual 62-0 vote — Haredi MKs voted with coalition. JPost "coalition falls to 48 seats" is polling projection for October 27 election, not actual coalition composition. i24NEWS "coalition majority dissolved" describes operational Haredi legislative boycott, not a formal majority-loss event. October 27 election date unchanged. Both YES criteria structurally foreclosed. ⚑ Human-review flag: verify no formal roll-call before July 17 dissolution.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a Knesset roll-call vote confirms coalition loss of majority (61 seats), OR if Netanyahu announces early dissolution and election date moves earlier than 2026-10-27. NO if coalition survives to mandatory election date with 61+ seats intact.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Knesset official record + Reuters/Haaretz/Times of Israel. Polling alone does not resolve.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If coalition drops below 61 but Netanyahu remains caretaker PM until election: YES. If a single party departs but coalition retains 61+: NO. Reviewed weekly only (Sundays); no intra-week deltas.</dd>
        </dl>
