  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>The Iran-Oman joint communiqué was published August 6 on Oman's Foreign Ministry website (fm.gov.om) and confirmed by Iran MFA spokesman Baghaei. The published text covers two items: agreement on geographic route coordinates for a navigable channel and establishment of a joint working group between the two FMs to determine "future administration of navigation, services and costs." No service fees, per-vessel charges, or cost schedule appear in the published text; Baghaei explicitly characterized the fee structure as deferred to the working group. The ambiguity rule — "service-fee outline without formal named agreement = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO" — is triggered. Forecast F1 closes RESOLVED-AMBIGUOUS, treated as NO. Successor forecast F8 opens at 38%, tracking whether the working group produces a named fee framework before August 22. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span>, opened <span class="cite">F8</span></p>
      <p>Trump cancelled the planned air campaign August 1 (confirmed: Axios, NPR, Washington Post, CBS). No US strikes on Iranian sovereign territory were recorded August 4–6 — six consecutive nights of the post-cancellation pause following the August 1 stand-down. Bessent's August 4 and 5 deal deadlines elapsed without strike or agreement. Iran's August 6 statement — that the US is "ready to return to commitments" under the June 17 MOU — is Iran's characterization of US posture, not a mutual announcement; it is consistent with active backchannel communication operating through the Oman channel. Five days remain on the August 11 horizon. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>
      <p>Iran MFA sustained its August 3 denial on August 6: "path of understanding is between Iran and Oman." The new formulation — US is "ready to return to commitments" — represents Iran's public framing of US posture, not a confirmation of a direct session. Qatar FM described the broader process as in "very progressive stages." The Iran-Oman joint working group creates a documented bilateral institutional channel that could, with Oman's facilitation, transition into a mediator-published readout satisfying F3's confirmation standard. Twelve days remain. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>
      <p>Kpler/AIS data for July 27–August 2 recorded 106 all-vessel Hormuz crossings across 96 distinct vessels (approximately 15 per day) — an all-vessel figure, not a commercial-transit count. TankerMap recorded zero tanker transits on August 5, against a 7-day all-vessel average of approximately one per day. Dark AIS accounted for 41% of crossings. P&amp;I war-risk cover remains suspended. The August 6 corridor communiqué establishes route coordinates but names no fees; insurance normalization and shipper-confidence recovery have not occurred. The resolution criterion requires 30 commercial transits per day on a 7-day rolling average — a threshold requiring structural normalization well beyond the current paper agreement. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
      <p>Channel 12's August 4 poll placed Likud and Eisenkot's Yashar each at 23 seats; JPost's August 4 poll placed the right bloc at approximately 50 seats total — eleven short of the 61-seat threshold — with Eisenkot leading Netanyahu by 10 points in PM preference and Beyachad (Bennett–Lapid) at 26 seats. Consistent right-bloc aggregates across multiple August polls show no convergence toward 61. No electoral pact or merger announced. 82 days remain before October 27. → moved <span class="cite">F6</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP (computed summary) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
