      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (12%):</strong> Residual US military strike on Iranian soil before August 11 (F2=12%); diplomatic track active via Oman but not sufficient to close the five-day window given Trump's documented reversal pattern.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (80%):</strong> Diplomatic channel holds via Oman intermediary; corridor route agreed, fees deferred to working group (F8=38%); no US strikes; commercial shipping normalization delayed past September 7 horizon (F4=8%); Iran-US mutual deterrence maintained without breakthrough on either axis.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (8%):</strong> Requires both formal Iran-US diplomatic session (F3=22%) and an operational named fee framework (F8=38%) to materialize within their respective horizons; computed as F3 &times; F8 &asymp; 8%.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media on August 6 framed the Iran-Oman joint communiqué as a bilateral sovereign achievement between two littoral states acting independently of "third parties." IRNA and Baghaei repeated the August 3 formulation verbatim: "path of understanding is between Iran and Oman." PressTV anchored the corridor framework in Iran's sovereign rights under international law, consistent with state-media positioning since February 2026. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>
      <p>The assertion that the US is "ready to return to commitments" serves a distinct domestic narrative function: it frames Trump's softened posture as capitulation to Iranian pressure rather than mutual de-escalation. The formulation allows the Iranian government to characterize diplomatic contact as American concession while maintaining the "no direct US talks" denial — Iran acknowledges US readiness as a concession extracted, not as a shared diplomatic position. This framing is internally consistent and has been applied without change since August 3. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>
      <p>On enrichment, state media characterized Iran's non-resumption of higher-level enrichment as a voluntary confidence-building gesture rather than a constraint. IAEA lack of access to Isfahan's underground HEU storage tunnels received no coverage. No HEU freeze mechanism or Nuclear Affairs working-group output was reported. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span> without move</p>
      <p>Knesset dissolution and Israeli election scheduling received minimal IRNA and PressTV coverage. Where it appeared, framing attributed Netanyahu's political fragility to the failure of Israel's military campaign rather than to domestic coalition dynamics. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

